A||||9||ChadMan||Friends from Louisville - please help!||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||07-01-2000||12:55 PM||||I dillied and dallied around making my hotel reservations for the FOCOA meet (7/27-7/30) and now the hotel is booked up.  FOCOA is staying at the Ramada on Riverside Drive, by the river in Jeffersonville, IN.<P>Where's the closest decent hotel to the Ramada?  I don't want to pay more than $100/night and a pool would be really nice since my Coupe has no air!<P>Thanks in advance for your help - I really appreciate it!||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||07-01-2000||01:29 PM||||hey ChadMan - my suggestion would be this -- call the Ramada back and see if they can book you a room at their sister hotel across the river -- it's located on Zorn Ave. which is a stones throw from the Jeff., IN hotel -- see if they will book you in there at the same rate (geezzzzzzz, they gotta have a provision for overflow and over bookings!!) -- talk nice to them and maybe they will do it for the same rate -- the Zorn Ave. property is on I-71 coming into Louisville and it's only about a mile before the split where you take I-65 across the river to the Jeff., IN Ramada.......give that a shot and see what happens.......||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||07-01-2000||02:36 PM||||i don't know if anything else is going on that week end (like a big convention or something) but louisville (right across the river is a big enough city that you should be able to find a room pretty easy. i don't stay in motels much, about 3 times in my life, but check any major chain for reservations in louisville, especially along i65 then it's just a strait shot across the bridge to jeff and the hotel (1st exit after the bridge). even if you can't get one along i65 louisville is pretty simply laid out highway wise so you could look or ask for something within the i264 loop (the watterson x-way) not the gene snyder loop (can't think of it's number), you'll be much further out. in fact, if you cant get into the main hotel i would say look for a hotel in the bardstown road - i264 area. not nessearily close to the hotel, but not more than about 15-20 min. away. i know there are at least 2 motel/hotels there but i can't say what they are, i do know one is a holiday inn. <P>that puts you close to a small mall a big theater complex both in walking distance. a decent map will get you to 2 larger malls, more or less by going the other way on i264 and just go up bardstown rd a few miles and end up in my favorite part of the city, the highlands for killing time and lots of resturants. you may want to do something other than hang around the remada for 2-3 days.<P>plus...and i didn't tell you this. the highlands is one of the places you'll find a lot of the import boys. a fiero parade would give them something to think about. no racing though, too busy.<P>i65 comes almost straight through the city so like i said, if you can stay near it or in and near the 264 (can't vouch for all areas of the city) loop a decent map (each year a local book map comes out. almost any store has them this year i think they're pink, about magazine size about $5) should have you navigating like a native (just practice saying louavul).  <BR>ok went and got a phone book but not really knowing hotels all i can say is there are plenty. and even though i like the bardstown rd. area staying somewhere in downtown louisville would be much closer since the city sits pretty much on the river. again, not knowing hotels i would say the brown on 4th st. looks ritzy though. don't know price.<P><BR>hope this helps or at least dosen't confuse you more.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-01-2000||03:12 PM||||Phillip, the Brown and the Gault House are both top line........I still think he should check out the Ramada on Zorn Ave. (I'm pretty sure it's a Ramada - if not, it is a Holiday Inn - I have stayed there and it's not pricy) it sits right at the intersection of Zorn and I-71 about a mile east of the Jeffersonville I-65 bridge -- that way he just drives a mile, crosses the bridge and he's there........||||reg||1
Z||000004||phillip||07-01-2000||03:12 PM||||tgowens probaly has the better idea. i do think if it can be arranged as many people who can't get into the remada should stay in some area where they are close to each other so you can help each other get there or at least be lost together.<P>i live with my brother and can't (and am not by nature anyway) be as hospitable as i'd like. i mean to show up there, but if you get lost or need help and i can offer it here are my various e-mail addys. i know i'll be working most of that weekend but i'll try to help.<P>philt2240@hotmail.com<BR>philt2240<BR>philphine<BR>rainseason@webtv.net<P>i don't have any pull with the local authorities or anything like that. you end up in jail...i don't know you. i'm not good buddies with any mechanics either. you'll have to bend over,same as me. seriously, i'll do what i can. <p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 07-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-01-2000||04:54 PM||||Chad--I can only assume that the FOCOA show is at the Expo center.  If it is, try a couple of motels south of town.  (The Expo center is south central L'ville.)  You might get a better (cheaper) deal and still be close to the action.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||07-01-2000||05:34 PM||||MM, the FOCOA show is at the Ramada Inn on I-65 in Jeffersonville, Indiana||||reg||1
